WEBVTT

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.570
Good morning, everyone!

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.570
Hero!

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.170
Good morning, Rona-chan!

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.830
A staff like this is a convenient thing 
to have when dungeon-crawling.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.720
Do you know why that is?

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.080
Go ahead, Princess Rona!

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.970
Huh?! Um...

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.200
You can use it to search for traps by 
poking the dungeon's walls and floors.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.720
Thank you so much.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:40.980
You can use it to search for traps by 
poking the dungeon's walls and floors!

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.230
I heard all that, you know.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.730
It's absolutely vital for adventurers 
to know how to use Cartado.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:57.980
They can be used for offensive magic like 
this, for carrying items, and more.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:58.740
Sensei.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.500
What <i>are</i> Cartado, exactly?

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.740
Well, you see...

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.180
Cartado dates back all the way

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.270
to ancient times, when 
Heaven and Earth were created.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.980
But there are various theories about that.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:17.040
One theory says the great creator appeared when our world was nothing but chaos—

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.000
no light, darkness, Heaven, or Earth—

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.400
and he raised one card 
and spoke, "Car Tado!"

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.760
In Ancient Lapanestan,
 this means "World, be filled with light!"

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.960
And the name "Cartado" is derived from that.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.030
Wow! Really?!

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.070
Hah!

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.780
Hey! Don't take over my lesson!

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.500
So good!

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.240
You're eating a lot again today, Fai-sama.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.790
Have some too, Princess.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.290
Thank you very much!

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:51.900
Our Fai is...

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.320
...sh-sharing food?

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.300
I guess they're real pals now.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.060
Wow, this ribbon's so cute!

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.820
It'll look good on you, Hero.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:11.930
I think it would look better on you.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:12.780
Huh?

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.230
You're really cute, after all!

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.340
My...

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.830
I had a very fulfilling day today.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.830
But... I feel as if something is missing...

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:35.360
That's right!

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.810
Endro!

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.560
What brings you here on our day off?

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.570
Sensei, the Hero isn't even slightly Heroic!

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:21.320
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.840
Heroes are exalted people who 
save the world from the heinous,

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:29.600
fiendish, good-for-nothing 
Demon Lord that brings chaos

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.330
and destruction to the world.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.210
Who're you calling "good-for-nothing"?!

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:35.210
What?

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.420
N-Nothing!

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.210
Continue.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.390
All right...

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:42.650
However, our Hero typically attends classes,

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:47.110
eats boxed lunches, goes shopping, 
and lives like a normal girl.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:50.840
You seem to be enjoying a lot of that 
yourself, though. Do you not like it?

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:54.350
It's not that I don't like it.
I'm having a lot of fun.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.360
Then what's the problem?

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:02.610
I still want to see the Hero
 doing Heroic things.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.560
Doing "Heroic things," huh?

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.220
Come to think of it,

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.620
she did say something about defeating 
an evil god over summer break.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.000
No idea if that's true, though.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:16.940
Defeating an evil god?! That's exactly it!

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.820
Give me more of that, please!

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.060
Are there any evil gods ripe 
to be defeated somewhere?

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:24.010
Of course not.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.590
And don't talk about evil 
gods as if they're fruit.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:31.770
Besides, even if she is the Hero, 
she's still just a fledgling.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:34.020
We can't let her go on Hero quests yet.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.440
Can't you do something about that?

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:39.380
I said no, and that means... no...

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:47.700
Sensei, is there nothing you can do?

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:52.580
No! I have a responsibility 
as a teacher... to...

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.830
All right. I'll help you.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:00.340
Sensei!

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.400
Thank you so much!

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.340
This is terrible!

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.340
The Demon Lord has revived 
and kidnapped Princess Rona!

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:11.220
What?!

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:14.540
The resurrected Demon Lord has 
erected a new Demon Lord Castle,

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.700
and he's waiting there for you, Hero.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.480
Since this is the Demon Lord,

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.980
only you, the wielder of the Hero's 
Sword, can save the Princess.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:26.740
Yulia Chardiet, go save Princess Rona!

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:27.750
Right!

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.490
<i>Of course, it's all an act...</i>

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.660
Everyone! We have to go save Rona-chan!

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.040
He can't get away with 
kidnapping the Princess!

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:38.890
We're up against the Demon Lord.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.670
We need to make sure we're prepared.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:44.920
This time, no Cartado will be held back!

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.940
<i>I feel bad watching them get so worked up.</i>

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.840
So the Demon Lord's finally appeared!

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.940
Yes. We'll need steel ourselves for this.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:52.930
<i>I'll apologize now. Sorry.</i>

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:51.820
No matter what enemies we'll face, I'll...

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:52.930
Yeah!

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.940
I just got back.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:02.190
Welcome back. How did it go?

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.950
Everything's all set.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.190
Yusha and the others are on their way here.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.620
My!

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:11.000
I'll finally get to see her being Heroic!

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.670
Still, I'm amazed you built this castle.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:18.210
I always thought a day like this might come...

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.460
So I had a Demon Lord Castle built!

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.920
What do you mean by "a day like this"?

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.090
Looks like they're here.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.010
Really?!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.530
Let's go, everyone!

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:35.100
Yeah!

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:43.810
Rona-chan, just wait for us!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.300
Be careful. We don't know 
where an enemy might attack—

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:49.110
...from?

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.320
A trap!

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.120
We should have brought that staff with us!

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:55.870
Everyone, run!

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.120
To that door!

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:03.810
Mei-chan!

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.130
Ow...

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:11.620
Huh?

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.270
This presence... It's a monster!

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.490
Sei-chan, Mei-chan, stay back!

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:21.270
Here it comes!

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:26.930
Pompom!

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:27.400
Huh?

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:29.530
Pomuruns?

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.780
They're really going at it.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:36.730
The Hero is fighting for me!

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:39.100
Wait, this isn't enough.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.900
Pomuruns won't work?

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.290
No. They're the weakest monster of all.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:47.820
And that last boulder trap 
was made out of papier-mâché.

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:49.920
And even now... Oh?

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.920
My, oh, my!

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.340
You even prepared recovery points for them?

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.300
This doesn't feel serious enough!

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:00.430
What do you want to do, then?

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:06.610
I believe the Hero should face trials
 like the ones spoken of in our legends.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:07.630
For example...

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.630
A falling trap that'll flatten even trolls!

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.880
An army of demons from the demon 
realm lying in wait for them!

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:18.950
Cursed evil spirits that'll steal their souls if 
they let their guard down for but a moment!

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:20.950
Things like that.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:24.080
Even I didn't set up hardcore stuff like that!

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:25.020
What?

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.830
N-Nothing!

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:32.710
Hey, Princess, do you want 
to put them all in danger?

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:36.970
Huh? Doesn't danger come with being the Hero?

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:43.330
Oh? But the one putting the Hero 
and her friends in danger is...

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.850
Huh? Huh? What?

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.110
Look. They're approaching the next room.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:56.930
My! I'll get to see the Hero's 
wonderful deeds this time!

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.620
You're certainly confident.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:09:59.530
Yes!

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:03.870
Because what awaits them next is 
the Demon Lord's Four Generals!

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:06.220
The Demon Lord's Four Generals?!

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.080
You actually got them?!

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:12.630
Who's there?!

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:23.010
Wait! What are those costumes?!

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:26.270
They're the Demon Lord's Four Generals. See?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:28.050
Perfect replicas.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.020
No, that's...

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:33.460
You can't just use that depiction as-is...

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.470
These people...

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:41.100
are really...

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:44.470
strong.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.040
That's the Four Generals for you.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:52.400
Wait, they're incredibly strong!

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:53.430
Of course.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:57.990
The ones in those costumes are my 
bodyguards and our nation's pride...

00:10:58.590 --> 00:10:59.620
Sword Master...

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.240
Grappler...

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:02.740
Archer...

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.180
and Arch Wizard.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.570
They're the strongest four people 
in the Lapanesta Kingdom.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:14.190
They might be even stronger 
than the real Four Generals.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.320
Is everyone all right?

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.590
This might be a bit too much.

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.950
Their strength's not even fair.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:29.960
The way this is going, we won't 
be able to save the Princess!

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:32.800
Not yet!

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:35.390
It's too early to give up!

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:41.890
Because we decided that we're going 
to save Rona-chan, no matter what!

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.610
Hero...

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:50.460
That's right.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.580
We're friends, after all.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:55.150
We can't let ourselves lose here!

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:57.150
Let's go, everyone!

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:58.300
Yeah!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.970
Stay out of our way!

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:21.180
We're... We're going to... save Rona-chan!

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:27.450
Huh?

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.300
Huh? What?

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.360
What's going on here?

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:40.190
You're letting us pass?

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:53.900
<i>The four of us have served the 
Princess since she was young.</i>

00:12:56.850 --> 00:13:00.120
Thank you for always protecting me.

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:05.030
<i>The Princess's happiness is all we wish for.</i>

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:10.000
<i>To have someone who cares for you so much...</i>

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:14.440
<i>You've made good friends, Princess.</i>

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.720
<i>ENDRO!</i>

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:28.320
It was wonderful seeing the Hero fight,

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:30.870
but it ended right at the good part.

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:35.460
I wonder why everyone stopped fighting...

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:40.000
Maybe they all suddenly got stomachaches?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.850
Princess Rona...

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:44.760
Yes?

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.390
Can we stop this already?

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:50.640
Huh?

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:56.800
I think you've already gotten your wish
 to see them fight like Heroes.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:00.150
You're satisfied now, right?

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:02.840
No!

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:06.050
After this comes their final battle
 against the Demon Lord.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:08.800
That's the climax of the any Hero's tale.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:11.910
It would be unthinkable to stop here.

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:13.360
Hmm...

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:17.670
Then what did you think as 
you watched them fight today?

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:18.510
Huh?

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.360
When they came for me...

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:27.930
I was truly happy.

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:31.200
I was nervous when they set off those traps,

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:36.210
and I was excited to see how truly 
wonderful their fighting was.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.630
But...

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:45.690
Because we decided that we're going 
to save Rona-chan, no matter what!

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:49.320
We're going to save Rona-chan!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:54.420
I wonder what it is...
 I feel this prickling in my chest.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.840
Even though I wanted to see my 
admired Hero in action so badly...

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.150
Then watch closely...

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.950
as the Demon Lord and Hero fight.

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:31.510
Sensei?

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:53.930
Rona-chan! We're here to save you!

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:55.640
Hero...

00:15:56.130 --> 00:16:00.010
You've done well to make it here, Hero.

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:02.690
Demon Lord! Give Rona-chan back!

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.540
Take that!

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:10.530
Huh?!

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.200
What is this?!

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:15.200
Why, you!

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.950
It's a barrier!
 One that's dangerously strong!

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:21.800
Seira-chan! Fai-chan! Mei-chan!

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:24.850
If you want to save her, 
you'll have to defeat me...

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:31.470
with your own power alone!

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.400
Hero...

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:35.550
Rona-chan...

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.040
Wait for me. I'll save you soon!

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:51.260
I ask of you: why do you seek the Princess?

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:54.610
For wealth? For status? For fame?

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:55.820
No!

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:58.530
Then is it because you're the Hero?

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:02.580
Because it's the Hero's destiny 
to defeat the Demon Lord?

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.000
It's none of those!

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:08.190
It's not because she's the Princess, 
or because I'm the Hero.

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:11.090
None of that matters.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:12.840
Rona-chan...

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:17.220
Rona-chan is our precious friend!

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:19.100
That's why I'm going to save her!

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.410
<i>That's right.</i>

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:24.670
<i>The Hero was always...</i>

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:26.450
<i>always...</i>

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:39.420
Rona-chan!

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:45.430
<i>She was always calling me "Rona,"
 and not "Princess."</i>

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.080
<i>But what about me?</i>

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.300
<i>I called her...</i>

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.740
Give Rona-chan back!

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:59.740
Please stop!

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:00.390
Huh?!

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:03.440
I'm sorry!

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.580
This was all my doing.

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:14.380
The Demon Lord's revival and 
my kidnapping were all lies.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:16.910
I'm truly sorry!

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:19.680
Huh?

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.040
Huh?

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.920
What?!

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:34.100
I've admired the Hero 
ever since I was little.

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:39.470
I thought that one day I would meet a Hero 
as lovely as the ones in the stories.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:44.460
But I've been too hung up on those stories

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:47.230
and never looked at what was really there.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:49.850
What was really there?

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:55.690
You, Hero... no, Yulia Chardiet-sama.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:59.280
I've constantly been imposing 
my ideal Hero upon you,

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.740
and I haven't been looking at the real you.

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:06.040
So you're saying you prepared a Demon 
Lord to make our Yusha act Heroic,

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.830
because she hasn't been Heroic at all?

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:13.130
That's true, though. 
Yusha-san's hardly Heroic.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.810
I can't really blame her.

00:19:14.810 --> 00:19:17.720
Huh?! That's not true!

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.020
That's right!

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:21.980
Yulia-sama is a wonderful person!

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:30.770
Anyway, I see. So there wasn't a Demon Lord.

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:32.660
Indeed.

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:33.850
That's good!

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:34.650
Huh?

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:37.930
I'm glad you weren't really kidnapped!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.320
Oh, but you know...

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:43.770
If the Demon Lord really did 
show up and kidnap you,

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.790
I'd definitely come save you again!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:47.440
Right!

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:48.520
Of course!

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:52.040
In fact, we should think of strategies 
to keep her from being kidnapped.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.230
Thank you so much, everyone!

00:19:57.680 --> 00:19:59.630
Hey, wait!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.710
Speaking of which, this person is...

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:03.550
A fake Demon Lord, right?

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:05.680
They were crazy strong, though.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:09.180
Um, who are you, exactly?

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:11.560
It's me!

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:15.820
See?

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.360
Mao-chan!

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.360
Mao-chan-sensei!

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.100
No way!

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:22.150
I didn't notice at all!

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.040
You used a transformation Cartado,

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:26.490
and a very high-powered one at that.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:30.090
I was seriously trying to cut through you!

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:31.750
I'm sorry!

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:33.200
Hmph.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:37.750
It'll be a hundred years before a weakling 
like you has the skill to slay me.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:38.760
Well, I'm off.

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:42.510
Don't be late tomorrow!

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:44.560
Okay!

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:50.020
Well, let's go home, Rona-chan!

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:54.560
Yes!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.930
I made you all lunches to 
apologize for the other day.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.750
Please eat them if you'd like.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.020
Yay!

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:10.140
You didn't have to go through the trouble.

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:14.670
A royal lunch!
 I bet it'll be incredibly luxurious!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.910
No, um...

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.300
It was my first time making anything,

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.420
so I hope you'll like them.

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:24.840
Wow! Incredible!

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.680
I'll have some!

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.930
I'll have some too, Princess.

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.180
So good!

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.190
They're good.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:41.440
Yeah, they're really good, Rona-chan!

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.480
Oh! I'm so glad!

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:46.200
Thank you so much, Yulia-sama!

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:47.140
Huh?

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:48.130
Huh?

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:51.520
"Yusha" is fine. You don't need to use "Yulia."

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:53.560
B-But...

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.000
Okay, Yusha-sama!

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:04.970
Roll 8 

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
Secret Cartado Festival!

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:38.940
"Secret Cartado Festival!"
